{"group_id": "re3d:Wikipedia:FD93899C448B33796DBBB7BBFEEFA3A6", "sample_id": "re3d:Wikipedia:FD93899C448B33796DBBB7BBFEEFA3A6:0:496", "source": "Wikipedia", "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yazidi_Book_of_Revelation", "target": {"location": ["the Yazidi village of Ba'idn", "Ba'id", "the village of Qasr 'tzz at-Din", "Qasr"], "money": [], "organization": ["Northern Kurdish", "text"], "person": [], "temporal": []}, "text": "The Yazidi Book of Revelation (Kitêba Cilwe in Kurdish; also transliterated as Kitab Al Jilwah) is one of two books on the Yazidi religion written in the style of a holy book in the Kurmanji dialect of the Northern Kurdish language, the other being the Yazidi Black Book (Mishefa Reş in Kurdish).[1] It is claimed that the original text of the Book of Revelation is kept in the Yazidi village of Ba'idn and the original text of the Yazidi Black Book is kept in the village of Qasr 'tzz at-Din.[2]"}
